  "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - x86 architecture;\n  - InfiniBand drivers;\n  - Network drivers;\n  - Mellanox network drivers;\n  - File systems infrastructure;\n  - IPv4 networking;\n  - Network traffic control;\n  - TCP network protocol;\n  - B.A.T.M.A.N. meshing protocol;\n  - IPv6 networking;\n  - Multipath TCP;\n  - Netfilter;\n  - RxRPC session sockets;\n  - SCTP protocol;\n  - SMC sockets;\n(CVE-2026-43083, CVE-2026-43197, CVE-2026-43198, CVE-2026-43465,\nCVE-2026-46242, CVE-2026-46325, CVE-2026-46331, CVE-2026-52914,\nCVE-2026-52924, CVE-2026-52931, CVE-2026-53151, CVE-2026-53176,\nCVE-2026-53212, CVE-2026-53215, CVE-2026-53225, CVE-2026-53228,\nCVE-2026-53359)\n",
  "id": "USN-8630-5",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in the Linux kernel.\n",
